  "answer": "Both files are in their final state. Let me confirm I haven't touched any other files by reviewing the ones I was told not to edit — they remain unchanged (I only read them).\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed route resolution in the request entry point by editing only the two writable files that were broken.\n\n### `entry.mjs` (production entry point)\n- **Removed the legacy short-circuit.** `dispatch` previously called `legacyResolve(path)` first, which incorrectly made the compatibility API part of production routing. Now `dispatch` delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`.\n- Input validation now flows through the resolver, so invalid paths throw `TypeError`.\n\n### `registry.mjs` (`resolveFromRegistry`)\nRewrote the matching loop to implement the required policy instead of naive first-match-in-declaration-order:\n- **Static beats dynamic regardless of order.** It scans all records, recording the first matching static and the first matching dynamic separately, then returns static first. This fixes the fixture's deliberate `/users/:id` (dynamic) before `/users/new` (static) ordering trap.\n- **Fallback is only used when nothing else matched.** Previously a fallback returned immediately on encounter, shadowing later static/dynamic matches. Now the first fallback is remembered and returned only if neither static nor dynamic matched.\n- **First-declared wins within a category** (first static, first dynamic, first fallback), and `null` is returned when there's no match and no fallback.\n- **Validation** explicitly rejects non-strings, empty strings, and paths not starting with `/` with a `TypeError`.\n- **Independence:** each call builds fresh `params` objects (`{}` literals / `matchDynamic`'s new object); records are never mutated.\n\n### Left unchanged (as required)\n- `legacy.mjs` — `legacyResolve` and its `/old/help` behavior are untouched.\n- `routes/static.mjs`, `routes/dynamic.mjs`, `routes/fallback.mjs` — support matchers already behave per spec (case-sensitive exact static match; dynamic requires whole nonempty segments and returns a fresh params object).\n- `fixtures/routes.mjs`, adapters (`http.mjs`, `cli.mjs`), and `utils/*` — untouched; they continue to work through the corrected entry point.\n\n### Verification (traced against the spec and `public.test.mjs`)\n- `dispatch('/users/new')` → `{ route: 'user-new', params: {} }` (static wins over earlier dynamic)\n- `dispatch('/users/Ada')` → `{ route: 'user-detail', params: { id: 'Ada' } }`\n- `dispatch('/missing')` → `{ route: 'not-found', params: {} }` (fallback)\n- `routeHttp('/health?q=one').match` → `{ route: 'health', params: {} }`\n- `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` → `null`\n- `dispatch(123)` / `dispatch('')` / `dispatch('users')` → `TypeError`\n\nNote: I could not execute the test runner (no shell tool available), so the above is a manual trace of the logic rather than an actual test run.",
